						"boxes" : [ 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-28",
									"linecount" : 8,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 31.25, 21.0, 598.0, 114.0 ],
									"text" : "I created this piece of music and named it Fireworks because its sound reminds me of a cherished memory from my childhood. During the Chinese New Year, it was a tradition for us to light firecrackers and fireworks, filling the air with their distinctive aroma. The scent of fireworks lingering in the air always reminded me of the comforting smell of geosmin after the rain—earthy and soothing.\n\nI will never forget how, as a small child, I would fall asleep to the rhythmic bursts of fireworks outside. Those sounds made me feel safe and at peace, wrapped in the joy and celebration of the festival. This piece captures that nostalgia, bringing back the warmth and serenity of those nights."
								}

							}
